她正试图教我怎么做。

00:29:36.460 --> 00:29:37.740
And I feel like she could defeat me.
我觉得她能打败我。

00:29:37.740 --> 00:29:45.059
I like, so the idea of doing a joke like that just rings so differently in my ears now and it feels a little, 20 years ago.
我——所以现在一想到要开那种玩笑，我听在耳朵里的感觉就完全不同了，会觉得有点20年前的感觉。

00:29:45.059 --> 00:29:47.299
It feels a little, my phone has internet now.
感觉有点像，我的手机现在能上网了。

00:29:47.299 --> 00:29:50.220
The level, not age and grade.
这是水平，而不是年龄和年级。

00:29:50.220 --> 00:30:02.126
But I do think that the show was always, is sometimes explicitly but most more implicitly asking questions about gender, what does it mean to be a man?
但我确实认为这部剧一直以来——有时是明确地，但更多时候是含蓄地——在探讨关于性别的问题：身为一个男人意味着什么？

00:30:02.126 --> 00:30:04.650
What does it mean to be a woman?
身为一个女人意味着什么？

00:30:04.650 --> 00:30:08.231
We showed strong women and we showed the softer side of men all the time.
我们一直都在展现坚强的女性，也展现男性温柔的一面。

00:30:08.231 --> 00:30:10.930
That's why that's another reason that joke isn't great.
这就是为什么——这也是那个笑话不太好的另一个原因。

00:30:10.930 --> 00:30:15.155
Who were trying to work through some of the masculine script.
我们当时正试图突破一些男子气概的陈规旧俗。

00:30:15.155 --> 00:30:27.069
I don't want to impose too much on this, but there's this kind of, I had said, I used to say that how I met your mother at it's heart was like a kind of gender flip, right?
我不想在这个问题上强加太多解读，但有这样一种——我以前常说，《老爸老妈浪漫史》的核心其实就像是一种性别翻转，对吧？

00:30:27.069 --> 00:30:34.549
You had Marshall and Ted being these incredibly sensitive guys who wanted to drink cocoa by the fire and be in relationships.
马修和特德是那种极其敏感的顾家好男人，他们想在壁炉旁喝热可可，渴望进入亲密关系。

00:30:34.549 --> 00:30:46.589
And then you had these women who were much more kind of no nonsense, like cut to the chase, not very sentimental, Lily and Robin.
而莉莉和罗宾则是那种更加务实、雷厉风行、不那么多愁善感的女性。

00:30:46.910 --> 00:30:50.670
And then you had Barney who was kind of this parody of hypermasculinity.
然后还有巴尼，他有点像是对极致男子气概的一种讽刺。

00:30:50.670 --> 00:30:51.222
Um, yeah.
嗯，对。

00:30:51.222 --> 00:31:02.269
So I think it was like trapped between two worlds in a way and that's where some of the detention exists, but also some of the unfortunate kind of, um, it was a negotiation, right?
所以我觉得它在某种程度上被夹在两个世界之间，这也是一些紧张感存在的地方，但同时也产生了一些不幸的……这是一个协商的过程，对吧？

00:31:02.269 --> 00:31:05.538
Because you guys were also trying to negotiate with the network.
因为你们当时也在努力跟电视台进行博弈。

00:31:05.538 --> 00:31:11.616
Like you wanted to be like seen as a tough cool show, but you also wanted to like put these vulnerable male characters.
比如，你们希望被视为一部硬核、酷炫的剧，但你们又想加入这些脆弱的男性角色。

00:31:11.616 --> 00:31:13.148
Like you centered them, right?
比如你们把他们作为核心，对吧？

00:31:13.148 --> 00:31:14.782
So it was always a tricky thing.
所以这一直是一件很棘手的事情。

00:31:14.782 --> 00:31:20.350
Like you weren't exactly smashing the patriarchy, but you were doing something revolutionary in your own way.
你们并非完全在粉碎父权制，但你们在用自己的方式做一些具有革命性的事情。

00:31:21.150 --> 00:31:22.881
Yeah, I definitely wanted to.
对，我绝对是这么想的。

00:31:22.881 --> 00:31:25.627
That was definitely the aesthetic of the show.
那绝对是这部剧的基调。

00:31:25.627 --> 00:31:28.492
And it is a gender flip right away in the pilot.
而且从试播集开始，它就是一个性别翻转。

00:31:28.492 --> 00:31:30.104
But Barney's Barney, right?
但巴尼就是巴尼，对吧？

00:31:30.104 --> 00:31:35.358
Barney will say and do things that are different from what Ted Marshall might say or do.
巴尼会说出、做出一些与特德或马修可能会说或做的话完全不同的事情。

00:31:35.358 --> 00:31:43.954
And just like Archie Bunker would say things on all in the family that his daughter and her husband found reprehensible and racist and terrible.
就像阿奇·邦克在《全家福》里说的话，他的女儿和女婿会觉得极其可憎、种族歧视且糟糕透顶。

00:31:43.954 --> 00:31:46.402
And Archie had to be Archie in that show.
但阿奇在那部剧里必须是阿奇。

00:31:46.402 --> 00:31:48.850
And Barney has to be Barney in this show.
而巴尼在这部剧里也必须是巴尼。

00:31:48.849 --> 00:31:52.904
And not everybody is equally as evolved in the way they speak about things.
并不是每个人在谈论事物时的开明程度都是一样的。

00:31:52.904 --> 00:31:59.932
And that sense, like, there's that weird thing of, if I'm being true to this character, they might say something like this, right?
从某种意义上说，就会有这样一种奇怪的情况：如果我要对这个角色保持真实，他们可能会说出这样的话，对吧？

00:31:59.932 --> 00:32:06.312
But then there's, if they say it too much and it feels like it's becoming literal, like it's the show's point of view.
但接着又会有另一种情况：如果他们说得太多，让人觉得这变成了字面意思，好像这就是整部剧的观点。

00:32:06.312 --> 00:32:07.447
That's when it's bad.
那才是糟糕的时候。

00:32:07.447 --> 00:32:11.610
You want it to be the character's point of you not to show his point of view.
你希望那是角色的观点，而不是剧集的观点。

00:32:11.610 --> 00:32:24.315
But I do think there's a kind of modern tendency that's not always unfortunate, but sometimes unfortunate, which is the idea that if a character in a show says something reprehensible, it's the point of view of the show or the writers.
但我确实认为有一种现代的倾向——它并不总是遗憾的，但有时是遗憾的——那就是认为，如果剧中的某个角色说了什么可憎的话，那就是整部剧或编剧的观点。

00:32:24.315 --> 00:32:26.099
And that's often not true at all.
而这通常根本不是事实。

00:32:26.099 --> 00:32:27.721
Like it's the opposite, right?
就像是恰恰相反，对吧？

00:32:27.721 --> 00:32:29.289
That's not how writing works.
写作可不是这么运作的。

00:32:29.289 --> 00:32:31.019
That's how writing works, right?
写作本来就该是这样的，对吧？

00:32:31.019 --> 00:32:33.830
That's there be no great, I think about Shakespeare.
否则就不会有什么伟大的作品了，我想到了莎士比亚。

00:32:33.830 --> 00:32:37.831
I think like, like, like Shakespeare's like, yeah, go like it makes sense.
我觉得，就像莎士比亚的剧作一样，对吧，说得通。

00:32:37.831 --> 00:32:41.399
Every greed work of art has a horrible character in it or several.
每一部伟大的艺术作品里都有一个或几个可怕的角色。

00:32:41.399 --> 00:32:41.899
Right?
对吧？

00:32:41.899 --> 00:32:42.439
And it is.
确实如此。

00:32:42.439 --> 00:32:42.939
Yeah.
对。

00:32:42.939 --> 00:32:44.021
It's an interesting.
这是一个很有趣的……

00:32:44.021 --> 00:32:47.859
You're always trying to find that level where you seem like you're not.
你总是在努力寻找那个平衡点：既要让剧集看起来没有在……

00:32:47.859 --> 00:32:52.617
The show is not endorsing a bad thing, but you're also being true to who a character is.
剧集没有在纵容一件坏事，但你同时也要忠于一个角色的真实性格。

00:32:52.617 --> 00:32:54.022
And that is a tough dance.
这是一支很难跳的舞。

00:32:54.022 --> 00:32:56.131
I won't say we got it right every time.
我不会说我们每次都做对了。

00:32:56.131 --> 00:33:10.890
Sometimes you, you hope that your audience sees it the way you do, and maybe most of the audience does, but some percentage of it hears it as the literal endorsement by the show as if the show is point of view is that that's when that's when I feel we we fail a little bit.
有时你会——你希望你的观众能以和你相同的方式来看待它，也许大多数观众确实如此，但总有一部分人会把它当作剧集的字面背书，仿佛剧集的观点就是那样——每当这个时候，每当我觉得我们稍微有点失败时。

00:33:10.890 --> 00:33:15.539
If too many people think that way, I think we we didn't communicate it clearly enough.
如果持这种想法的人太多，我觉得就是我们没有表达得足够清楚。

00:33:15.539 --> 00:33:28.785
I think some of that happened sometimes with Barney and in other ways, but I like to think that, for example, with Barney, he mostly plays as a parody of something, not an endorsement of something, but I know that not everybody took it that way.
我觉得巴尼身上有时确实发生过这种情况，其他方面也是如此，但我愿意相信，以巴尼为例，他主要起到的是一种讽刺的作用，而不是对某种行为的纵容，但我知道并不是每个人都这么想的。

00:33:28.380 --> 00:33:29.256
That was the intention.
但这确实是我们的初衷。

00:33:29.256 --> 00:33:29.980
It's all I can say.
我只能说这些了。

00:33:29.980 --> 00:33:31.539
All right, that's what I got for this week.
好了，这就是我这周要分享的内容。

00:33:31.539 --> 00:33:32.500
Great questions.
精彩的问题。

00:33:32.500 --> 00:33:33.339
Great question.
好问题。

00:33:33.339 --> 00:33:35.259
Thank you for those questions.
谢谢你们提出这些问题。

00:33:35.259 --> 00:33:39.099
Hey, Craig, you having a good time doing this podcast?
嘿，克雷格，你录这个播客录得开心吗？

00:33:39.099 --> 00:33:40.259
I'm having a really good time, Trins.
我录得非常开心，特兰斯。

00:33:40.259 --> 00:33:41.099
I like it.
我很喜欢。

00:33:41.099 --> 00:33:42.339
You have a good time doing this podcast.
你录这个播客录得挺开心吧。

00:33:42.339 --> 00:33:42.859
I better be.
我最好是开心。

00:33:42.859 --> 00:33:44.099
It's all I do.
这就是我全部的活儿了。

00:33:44.099 --> 00:33:45.099
Yeah.
对。

00:33:45.099 --> 00:33:48.859
Well, I am, I am, and we're so grateful.
嗯，我是，我是，我们非常感激。

00:33:48.859 --> 00:33:54.900
A lot of people are listening and writing in, and it just feels like we're getting to sit around a campfire and share these, how I made my mother's story.
很多听众都在收听并来信分享，这感觉就像我们围坐在篝火旁，分享这些“我是如何创作我母亲的故事”的经历。

00:33:54.900 --> 00:33:56.940
So thank you for joining us.
所以谢谢你们加入我们。

00:33:56.940 --> 00:33:59.259
Thank you for continuing to journey with us.
谢谢你们继续与我们同行。

00:33:59.259 --> 00:34:02.940
We got a lot more to go, but it's been a blast, so thanks a lot.
我们还有很长的路要走，但这非常有趣，非常感谢。

00:34:02.940 --> 00:34:05.339
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:34:05.339 --> 00:34:07.220
Please equip me.
请武装我。

00:34:07.220 --> 00:34:12.010
Olsen's off again in New York City.
奥尔森又去了纽约市。

